in public education there are a lot of  different ideas about what the purpose  of education is if you ask any student  or even a lot of parents  they immediately start talking about  getting a job  security for the future and kids will  say the purpose of education is to get  rich that sounds good on the surface but  what it yields is an education system  that asks sixth graders to figure out  what they're gonna be when they grow up  and so you get schools where  teachers are there to sort of supervise  and  guide but not to teach directly as a  mother  i wanted  much more than that for my children i  didn't want them to go through an  education system  i wanted them to be  educated  if you come to one of the hillsdale  classical schools you will see  all kinds of things going on that just  don't go on in public schools anymore  [Music]  in the hillsdale classical school we are  training the minds and the hearts of our  students  we're training them to think well and  we're training them to love the right  things  we want our students to learn to be  virtuous people and we want them to be  knowledgeable people and we want them to  spend their lives pursuing the good even  if we produce students who don't know  everything if we produce students who  have the disposition to continue  learning and teaching themselves and  pursuing knowledge  then we've done a good job  way to go good morning  [Music]  sometimes people think that classical  education is really elite and fancy and  only for a certain group of students  and that's not true if you look at the  history of education in this country you  see that a couple generations ago  everyone was learning to diagram  sentences everyone was learning cursive  lots of people were learning latin  there's a difference of course between  the great minds that we study and  ourselves  but it's not that the great minds are  the only ones who can understand these  things we can too the difference is the  great minds are the ones 