 is not just for the sake of a  job education is learning for the sake  of learning  i didn't know going into hillsdale  really what classical education was and  so i felt behind  you know a lot of the students there  already had been reading  aristotle and plato and all of these  great thinkers  and i hadn't read them and so i didn't  know  what a lot of those things meant  and what it meant to  have an education like this  asking these big questions and these  really important books has led me to  you know think about my future and in  doing so i think that i want to continue  pursuing these big questions and things  that i care about and so i think when i  go to college i want to pick a college  that really cares about the  formation of the soul and not just you  know  a job training so a student who walks  all the way through and receives a  classical education by the time they're  graduating from a school like ours  i think they really have wisdom well  beyond their age  in part because they've become in a  sense the things that they've beheld  and what we see is  people who aren't confident without  being arrogant  people who are well spoken  and who think that their lives have a  purpose  and who feel equipped to  begin pursuing happiness in the best way  [Music]  [Music]  we have parents who come in all the time  thinking oh my goodness wow this is  amazing what they are doing can my child  do this too and i look at them and i say  absolutely i teach here and i teach in  general because i want to see the kids  learn and watching them having that  moment of understanding and of clarity  that makes everything worth it i think  my hope for them is  they would be  more fully human when they leave here  i hope that these schools will remind  people that these classical methods  are worth pursuing because  they work  and that as a country  our future depends  on  raising a generation of young people  who  know how to think and read  and write and spend their lives